# Electromagnetism 03 — A series RLC circuit rings down
#
# A 20.0 μF capacitor is charged to V₀ = 10.0 V and, at t = 0, connected across a
# 50.0 mH inductor and a 20.0 Ω resistor in series. Kirchhoff's loop rule gives
#
#     L q'' + R q' + q/C = 0,    q(0) = C V₀,  q'(0) = 0.
#
# (a) Find the undamped frequency ω₀ = 1/√(LC), the damping rate α = R/2L and the
#     damped frequency ω_d = √(ω₀² − α²).
# (b) Solve for q(t) and find the charge and the current at t = 2.00 ms. Compare with
#     q(t) = Q₀ e^(−αt) (cos ω_d t + (α/ω_d) sin ω_d t).
# (c) How much energy has the resistor turned into heat by t = 10.0 ms? Compare
#     ∫ i² R dt with the drop in stored energy, q²/2C + L i²/2.
# (Halliday/Resnick ch. 31, Purcell & Morin ch. 8)

C = 20.0 μF
V0 = 10.0 V
L = 50.0 mH
R = 20.0 Ω
Q0 = C V0

# (a)
ω0 = 1 / √(L C)
α = R / (2*L)
ω_d = √(ω0² - α²)
print "ω0  =", ω0 in rad/s to 8 digits
print "α   =", α in 1/s to 8 digits
print "ω_d =", ω_d in rad/s to 8 digits

# (b) Kirchhoff's loop rule
solve L q'' + R q' + q / C = 0
  with q(0) = Q0, q'(0) = 0 A
  for t from 0 ms to 10 ms
q_exact(t) = Q0 exp(-α t) (cos(ω_d t) + α / ω_d * sin(ω_d t))
t1 = 2.00 ms
print "q(2 ms) solve =", q(t1) in μC to 8 digits
print "q(2 ms) exact =", q_exact(t1) in μC to 8 digits
print "i(2 ms) solve =", q'(t1) in mA to 8 digits
print "i(2 ms) exact =", q_exact'(t1) in mA to 8 digits

# (c) energy: the heat from the numerical current, and from the exact one
t2 = 10.0 ms
heat = ∫ q'(t)² R dt from 0 ms to t2
heat_exact = ∫ q_exact'(t)² R dt from 0 ms to t2
U(t) = q(t)² / (2*C) + ½ L q'(t)²
print "heat in R by 10 ms (solve) =", heat in mJ to 8 digits
print "heat in R by 10 ms (exact) =", heat_exact in mJ to 8 digits
print "drop in stored energy      =", U(0 ms) - U(t2) in mJ to 8 digits
